Fix the book-language issue shown in the latest screen recording.

Observed problem:
- the book landing page could show Chinese headings while the cover and epigraph remained English;
- the prologue could show Chinese UI while the body stayed English;
- later chapters already behaved better because they were using a versioned reader URL.

Root cause:
- the book-specific scripts trusted the static HTML `lang` before the actual language selector / saved RUNLU language;
- early book pages were still loading unversioned reader scripts;
- translation text fetches used `force-cache`, which could preserve stale chapter text after editorial updates.

Fix:
- prioritize RUNLU runtime language, selector, and saved language before static HTML fallback;
- change translation fetches to normal revalidation (`no-cache`);
- bump the book landing script and all reader pages from Prologue through Chapter 10 to `v=3` so browsers fetch the corrected scripts immediately.

Scope: only files under `book/`. No unrelated RUNLU, Flooring OS, Invoice, LINGGUANG, or homepage changes.

